course: dictionary
lesson: 12440
title: Breaking the code
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Decipherment means working out what a code, a secret message or hard-to-read old writing says. «The detectives spent all night on the decipherment of the secret note.» They were not reading an ordinary note. They were turning strange signs into real words.
explain: Clues help with decipherment. Look for signs that repeat and ask what they might stand for. «The message used one strange symbol again and again.» A symbol that keeps coming back is a clue, just as a repeated word can be a clue in a story.
explain: Decipherment is slow, careful work. Try one idea, check whether it makes sense, and if it does not, try another idea.
fact: Decipherment means working out the meaning of a code, secret message or old writing that is hard to read.
fact: «Decipher» is the verb: to decipher a message means to work out what it says.
fact: The Rosetta Stone helped scholars with the decipherment of Egyptian hieroglyphs, and Jean-François Champollion announced his decipherment in 1822.
fact: At Bletchley Park, people worked on the decipherment of coded messages during the Second World War.
fact: In puzzles and olympiads, decipherment means solving an unknown script step by step.
exercise: «The detectives spent hours on the decipherment of the secret note.» What does decipherment mean here? | Writing a new note to a friend | Hiding the note under the bed | *Working out what the secret note says | Tearing the note into small pieces
exercise: «The old letters were written in a script nobody could read.» Find and copy one word that means a style of writing. | nobody | *script | letters | written
exercise: Ella says decipherment is losing a message in the post. What is it really? | Sending a message very quickly | Losing a message in the post | Drawing a picture of a message | *Working out the meaning of a hard-to-read message
test: «Champollion's decipherment of hieroglyphs was announced in 1822.» What does decipherment mean in this sentence? | Writing a new language from scratch | Painting the walls of a temple | Burying old stones in the desert | *Working out the meaning of the hieroglyphs
test: Which clue helps most in decipherment? | Guessing one random letter and never trying another | Asking nobody and waiting for the answer | Ignoring every symbol that repeats | *Noticing a symbol that appears again and again
exam: Mina says, «Decipherment is the hard job of working out a secret message.» Which word is closest in meaning to decipherment? | *Code-breaking | Decorating | Forgetting | Guessing
